++# Local browser prototype
++
++This is an unpublished acquisition prototype using the existing 0.9.2 package.
++Files are read with File.arrayBuffer and processed in a disposable Worker;
++there is no upload/analytics code. PDF preview availability depends on the
++browser's PDF viewer. Inputs have a compressed-size cap; ZIP inflation and XML
++resource admission still depend on the engine and must be hardened before an
++untrusted-input production launch. Process cancellation terminates the worker.
++
++The Vite console-pipe plugin is configured for terminal-visible development
++console logs. Pin the resolved dependencies in the lockfile when implementing.
++The plugin is disabled by its own production-build behavior.
++
++```sh
++npm --prefix examples/playground install
++npm --prefix examples/playground run build
++npm --prefix examples/playground run dev
++```
++
++The implementation milestone must add sample inputs, a sample-first path,
++copy-snippet controls, terminal-captured browser smoke, request-body inspection,
++keyboard/accessibility checks and Chromium/Firefox integration. This prototype
++is complete for local file selection/render/compare/cancel/download, but does
++not claim those product/verification tasks are already done.
